advertised metadata (the builtin table row)
-------------------------------------------

name          list_sessions
description   "List Isabelle sessions known to the server (from ROOT
              files on the configured dirs — the distribution, and
              the AFP if registered), optionally glob-filtered by
              name. Each entry: name, chapter, one-line description,
              whether a built heap exists, and a marker on the
              session the server is running as base image. Sessions
              are the unit of coarse-grained availability: theories
              of the base image are queryable now; others need
              load_theory (fine-grained, slow) or a heap build +
              server restart (coarse-grained). Follow with
              list_theories for a session's contents."
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {"pattern": {"type": "string"}}}
              (no required — bare call lists everything.)
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": true, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}
outputSchema  none.

